+Preview navigation synchronizes by document headings. The active section is the
+last heading at or before the cursor, including nested headings. Crossing into a
+different section in either source or preview moves the other visible buffer to
+that heading; moving within a section leaves it alone. Opening or toggling back
+lands at the selected heading, rather than the exact paragraph or column.
+Documents without headings and text before the first heading use document start.
+Repeated heading titles remain separate sections, including after table or
+Mermaid expansion. Long headings retain their Markdown syntax and can be read
+with horizontal scrolling in the preview.
+
 # Completions
 
